  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "Compute the sum of all the roots of \\((2x+3)(x-4)\\) \\(+(2x+3)(x-6)=0.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\)",
    "E": "\\(13\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Both terms contain \\(2x+3\\), so factoring out this repeated expression turns the equation into a product:\n\\[\n(2x+3)\\bigl((x-4)+(x-6)\\bigr)\n=(2x+3)(2x-10)=0.\n\\]\nA product is zero exactly when at least one factor is zero. Thus all the roots come from\n\\[\n2x+3=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2x-10=0,\n\\]\nwhich give \\(x=-\\frac32\\) and \\(x=5\\). Their sum is\n\\[\n-\\frac32+5=\\frac72.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac72}\\), choice A.",
